    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "2KI 3:8",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then he said, “Which way shall we go up?” Jehoram answered, “The way of the wilderness of Edom.”",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "ff9f1ff3d927b74166667a2b5a9a516925a2bb7a66a81f4a310cd2addfe5c7d8",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI03.htm#V8"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 3:9",
        "textualBasisJa": "So the king of Israel went with the king of Judah and the king of Edom, and they marched for seven days along a circuitous route. There was no water for the army or for the animals that followed them.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "9a9b825534623dad87fedd78b8a9ac5a4a774db154adaf0cef4d715d05fb3a0c",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI03.htm#V9"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 3:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "Jehoshaphat said, “The LORD’s word is with him.” So the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat and the king of Edom went down to him.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "61e4ca6835ed42fb88a19a111610b1100f518cae3d99535d4c56394f9b8719e5",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI03.htm#V12"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 3:20",
        "textualBasisJa": "In the morning, about the time of offering the sacrifice, behold, water came by the way of Edom, and the country was filled with water.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "e11aa2abe76ba4690fad77c8a1da5945bb03cf005d64d393333ff57d23c390b6",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI03.htm#V20"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 3:26",
        "textualBasisJa": "When the king of Moab saw that the battle was too severe for him, he took with him seven hundred men who drew a sword, to break through to the king of Edom; but they could not.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "683f09a28237edbbdc6b0cad07f8217b524c43f0083cff68a7774ab75825d95f",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI03.htm#V26"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 8:20",
        "textualBasisJa": "In his days Edom revolted from under the hand of Judah, and made a king over themselves.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "24461c351cf0da21f1ef64702fee29a751b18b9278ced29dffe4816aff82b70f",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI08.htm#V20"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 8:22",
        "textualBasisJa": "So Edom revolted from under the hand of Judah to this day. Then Libnah revolted at the same time.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "60336f7122245b9f1c0efa4eb0f424942aabd4e2db0fa9905cf3abac06ac74a5",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI08.htm#V22"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 14:10",
        "textualBasisJa": "You have indeed struck Edom, and your heart has lifted you up. Enjoy the glory of it, and stay at home; for why should you meddle to your harm, that you fall, even you, and Judah with you?”",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "ca1e004be2c8c37b9aeabdfba9cb5be90e1a7d029c7c50225c9df31197bb2a73",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/2KI14.htm#V10"
      }
